.TH V32IO.HPP 3v32 "October 14, 2026" "v32c++ 20261014-dev" "v32c++ Library"
.SH NAME
v32/v32io.hpp \- v32::IoDevice, a gamepad port read as v32io data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <v32/v32io.hpp>
.PP
.B namespace v32 {
.PP
.B "enum GamepadPort { FirstGamepadPort = 0, SecondGamepadPort = 1,"
.B "                   ThirdGamepadPort = 2, FourthGamepadPort = 3 };"
.PP
.B "enum IoControl {"
.B "    IoLeft = 1,    IoRight = 2,  IoUp = 4,   IoDown = 8,"
.B "    IoStart = 16,  IoA = 32,     IoB = 64,   IoX = 128,"
.B "    IoY = 256,     IoL = 512,    IoR = 1024, IoAll = 2047"
.B "};"
.PP
.B class IoDevice {
.BI "    IoDevice( int " gamepad " );"
.B  "    int  port();"
.B  "    bool probe();"
.B  "    int  read();"
.B  "    int  read_previous();"
.B  "    int  changed();"
.BI "    bool is_down( int " mask " );"
.B  "    bool connected();"
.B  "    bool plugged();"
.B  "    int  scan();"
.B };
.PP
.B }
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Vircon32 console has no keyboard or mouse port.
.I v32io
connects them through a gamepad port instead: the console sees a
gamepad, but its 11 controls carry keyboard or mouse data, which the
drivers in
.BR keyboard.hpp (3v32)
and
.BR mouse.hpp (3v32)
decode.
.B IoDevice
is the core they share: it reads a gamepad's 11 controls and packs them
into one
.BR int ,
one bit per control
.RB ( IoControl ),
in the order of the console's input ports. Use it directly to write a
driver of your own or to look at what a device is sending.
.PP
This is a C++ port of the v32io C drivers
.RI ( https://github.com/wedge1020/v32io ),
using the same protocols and decoding. It does not need the C library,
and the two are not meant to be mixed in one program.
.SS Requirements
A v32io device must be attached; without one this header does nothing
useful. Either:
.IP \(bu 2
the v32io hardware adaptor, which presents a USB keyboard or mouse to
the computer as a joystick named
.B v32io:kbd
or
.BR v32io:mouse ,
mapped in any Vircon32 emulator with a joystick profile that sends
button
.I n
to control
.IR n ;
or
.IP \(bu 2
a modified Vircon32 emulator with the
.B v32kbd
and
.B v32mouse
devices in its
.B Gamepads
menu (see
.BR Vircon32 (1)).
.PP
The stock emulator's
.B Keyboard
device is not a v32io keyboard: it maps a few keys to gamepad buttons,
and reads as garbage here. Port ids count from 0; the emulator's menus
count gamepads from 1.
.SS The rule
Call
.B probe
once on
.B every
frame, for every device, before
.BR end_frame .
The console updates the gamepads only between frames, and a keyboard
reports at most one key event per frame, so a skipped frame can lose a
key or misread mouse movement. Extra calls in the same frame do
nothing.
.SS Members
.TP
.B IoDevice( gamepad )
Read gamepad port
.I gamepad
(0 to 3). The constructor writes a small machine-code routine into the
object that reads all 11 ports in one call, and takes what the device
shows right now as the starting state.
.TP
.B port
The gamepad port.
.TP
.B probe
Read the controls, keeping the previous reading. Returns true when the
packed controls changed. A second call in the same frame returns false
and reads nothing.
.TP
.BR read ", " read_previous
The packed controls from the latest probe, and from the one before.
.TP
.B changed
The controls that changed in the latest probe, as
.B IoControl
bits.
.TP
.B is_down
Whether any control in
.I mask
was held at the latest probe.
.TP
.B connected
Whether the gamepad was connected at the latest probe.
.TP
.B plugged
Whether the gamepad became connected at the latest probe. A newly
connected gamepad shows every control released whatever the device
holds, so protocols that depend on history start over.
.TP
.B scan
Read the controls now, without touching the probe history. Drivers use
.B probe
instead.
.PP
Every method restores the previously selected gamepad.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the raw bits a device sends on gamepad 2 (port 1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
#include <v32/v32io.hpp>
#include <v32/string.hpp>

v32::IoDevice device( v32::SecondGamepadPort );

void main()
{
    while( true )
    {
        device.probe();

        v32::String bits( "" );
        bits.append_int( device.read(), 2 );
        clear_screen( color_black );
        bits.print_at_xy( 10, 10 );
        end_frame();
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keyboard.hpp (3v32),
.BR mouse.hpp (3v32),
.BR input.h (3v32),
.BR Vircon32 (1),
.BR v32c++\-headers (3v32)
.PP
.I docs/V32IO.md
in the v32c++ source distribution, and the v32io repository,
.IR https://github.com/wedge1020/v32io .
.SH AUTHOR
Matthew Haas
